{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21ef7e39d99b57bc5aef", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Electromagnetic Induction - Test 2", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 50, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926ebd9"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb93", "title": "Physics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb2c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e0"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8edd"], "question": {"text": "A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> battery connected to a coil of resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8486;</mo></math> through a switch, drives a constant current in the circuit. The switch is opened in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ms</mi></math>. The emf induced across the coil is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. The inductance of the coil is :"}, "options": [{"id": "049cc6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mH</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb2d"}, {"id": "de9271", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mH</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb2e"}, {"id": "0bc661", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mH</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb2f"}, {"id": "883a92", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mH</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb30"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb31", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b89"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95c4"], "question": {"text": "A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> long horizontal wire extends from North East to South West. It is falling with a speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5.0</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></math> at right angles to the horizontal component of the earth&#39;s magnetic field of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0.3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Wb</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> The value of the induced emf in the wire is:"}, "options": [{"id": "b2e7cc", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0.3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb32"}, {"id": "0a64b7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1.1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb33"}, {"id": "e6287b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2.5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb34"}, {"id": "6fe57b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1.5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb35"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb36", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5e"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b564a"], "question": {"text": "An inductance coil has a reactance of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> . When an AC signal of frequency&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math> is applied to the coil, the applied voltage leads the current by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. The self-inductance of the coil is"}, "options": [{"id": "233ea5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb37"}, {"id": "49fcec", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb38"}, {"id": "b33b2d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb39"}, {"id": "bc6a71", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb3a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb3b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f87fe"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87ce"], "question": {"text": "An inductor coil stores <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>64</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> of magnetic field energy and dissipates energy at the rate of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>640</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math> when a current of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is passed through it. If this coil is joined across an ideal battery, find the time constant of the circuit (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>).<br />&nbsp;"}, "options": [{"id": "0c3da6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb3c"}, {"id": "89e4b4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb3d"}, {"id": "9b9024", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>125</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb3e"}, {"id": "cb90fe", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb3f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb40", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b566e"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5644"], "question": {"text": "<p>The source of time varying magnetic field may be</p><p>(A) a permanent magnet</p><p>(B) an electric field changing linearly with time</p><p>(C) direct current</p><p>(D) a decelerating charge particle</p><p>(E) an antenna fed with a digital signal</p><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "a358c1", "text": "(C) and (E) only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb41"}, {"id": "55832b", "text": "(D) only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb42"}, {"id": "a611dc", "text": "(A) only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb43"}, {"id": "fa513f", "text": "(B) and (D) only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb44"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb45", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60ced5dc19d2aa2b78a3a76c"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8ed4"], "question": {"text": "A <math><mn>20</mn></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>H</mtext></math> inductor coil is connected to a <math><mn>10</mn></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;resistance in series as shown in figure. The time at which rate of dissipation of energy&nbsp;(Joule&#39;s heat)&nbsp;across resistance is equal to the rate at which magnetic energy is stored in the inductor, is:<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F36cb4009-f746-4169-87cb-d4cdb6e75f7c-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 180px;\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "b905d8", "text": "<math> <mfrac>  <mn>1</mn>  <mn>2</mn> </mfrac> <mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb46"}, {"id": "754e42", "text": "<math> <mn>2</mn><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb47"}, {"id": "c330fa", "text": "<math> <mfrac>  <mn>2</mn>  <mrow>   <mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow> </mfrac> </math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb48"}, {"id": "7e8a77", "text": "<math> <mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb49"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb4a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b89"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b5c"], "question": {"text": "A uniform magnetic field of 0.4 T acts perpendicular to a circular copper disc 20 cm in radius. The disc is having a uniform angular velocity of $10 \\pi \\mathrm{rad} \\mathrm{s}^{-1}$ about an axis through its centre and perpendicular to the disc. What is the potential difference developed between the axis of the disc and the rim ? $(\\pi=3.14)$"}, "options": [{"id": "582e10", "text": "$0.5024 \\mathrm{~V}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb4b"}, {"id": "10ba05", "text": "$\\mathrm{~V}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb4c"}, {"id": "353a4d", "text": "$0.2512 \\mathrm{~V}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb4d"}, {"id": "cbfe7d", "text": "$0.1256 \\mathrm{~V}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb4e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb4f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1e66f9ce3f243b4b18"], "question": {"text": "<p>A small square loop of wire of side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math>&nbsp;is placed inside a large square loop of wire <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>&#8811;</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. Both loops are coplanar and their centres coincide at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math> as shown in figure. The mutual inductance of the system is</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fbb2446ca-823a-4a72-bf46-3cc1db8f0449-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 170px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "92fa06", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb50"}, {"id": "c97404", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb51"}, {"id": "a59b22", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb52"}, {"id": "b8c9a6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb53"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb54", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e0"], "concepts": ["60e5678c499d1e49588f9257"], "question": {"text": "A coil is placed perpendicular to a magnetic field of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5000</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>. When the field is changed to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3000</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>, an induced emf of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>22</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> is produced in the coil. If the diameter of the coil is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>02</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>, then the number of turns in the coil is:"}, "options": [{"id": "f253d9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb55"}, {"id": "fa934c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>70</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb56"}, {"id": "547cbe", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>35</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb57"}, {"id": "a4d864", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>140</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb58"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb59", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f87fe"], "concepts": ["6162fb3b6ed13040ec84c84c"], "question": {"text": "<p>For the plane electromagnetic wave given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;the&nbsp;ratio of average electric energy density to average magnetic energy density is&nbsp;</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "629d84", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb5a"}, {"id": "1f8eca", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb5b"}, {"id": "399daf", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb5c"}, {"id": "c0c71e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb5d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb5e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60ced5dc19d2aa2b78a3a76c"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8ed4"], "question": {"text": "In the circuit shown,<br><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FkbMOwC2aGptvR-vCPHDwKsu6UBwKW6tfmxuZxxHuFDM.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>the switch $S_{1}$ is closed at time $t=0$ and the switch $S_{2}$ is kept open. At some later time $\\left(\\mathrm{t}_{0}\\right)$, the switch $\\mathrm{S}_{1}$ is opened and $\\mathrm{S}_{2}$ is closed. the behaviour of the current I as a function of time ' $\\mathrm{t}$ ' is given by:"}, "options": [{"id": "8d5456", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FWUqWNjx0bipGRxfznfB2BlAKR_19TssDxkWy4ket2Fg.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\">", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb5f"}, {"id": "47200b", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F27kdZt6lTf6FSkLIYCyv15tlBnDDzXqnxirGdXoEiUM.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\">", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb60"}, {"id": "c15cef", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fv6PwSrKR9YF5OZFYP7QQ60R1iwYwoDna_wkG7ob_4rE.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\">", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb61"}, {"id": "98b859", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F8zK6dkfoce0avAsTOdFUZ6KRpSqiy_baFKegII0BBB0.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\">", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb62"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb63", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e0"], "concepts": ["60ced5db19d2aa2b78a3a73a"], "question": {"text": "<p>A bar magnet is passing through a conducting loop of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> with velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The radius of the bar magnet is such that it just passes through the loop. The induced e.m.f. in the loop can be represented by the approximate curve:</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fc88b273c-a99c-4166-b77e-5bfdacc51392-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 102px; height: 161px;\" />&nbsp;<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F6afea83f-af2a-4000-a59f-fd8f0e28909f-b2909a94-b955-4119-8168-9f16585efe92-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 290px; height: 194px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "3a1809", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F89257063-8a5e-44b3-8107-9fef30547eb1-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 337px; height: 225px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb64"}, {"id": "dbf1ae", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fe5e21bb4-3fd8-4bf2-b8ef-f0e24a70f544-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 341px; height: 227px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb65"}, {"id": "bf5444", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F16fe1ffe-6580-41b9-aca4-066f4345a16d-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 341px; height: 229px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb66"}, {"id": "9424b5", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F27554301-3d14-4a27-b0bd-f70c0443adb9-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 341px; height: 229px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb67"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb68", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b89"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95c4"], "question": {"text": "A square loop of side $15 \\mathrm{~cm}$ being moved towards right at a constant speed of 2 $\\mathrm{cm} / \\mathrm{s}$ as shown in figure. The front edge enters the $50 \\mathrm{~cm}$ wide magnetic field at $t=$ 0 . The value of induced emf in the loop at $t=10 \\mathrm{~s}$ will be :\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FXgs8Q8Qun4rlgV327RmadPvLXnHTCpiLCQjSDvyshEk.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>"}, "options": [{"id": "b186e3", "text": "$0.3 \\mathrm{mV}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb69"}, {"id": "dae16e", "text": "zero", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb6a"}, {"id": "830e40", "text": "$4.5 \\mathrm{mV}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb6b"}, {"id": "c003a1", "text": "$3 \\mathrm{mV}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb6c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb6d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5e"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b564a"], "question": {"text": "Regarding self-inductance:\nA. The self-inductance of the coil depends on its geometry.\nB. Self-inductance does not depend on the permeability of the medium.\nC. Self-induced e.m.f. opposes any change in the current in a circuit.\nD. Self-inductance is electromagnetic analogue of mass in mechanics.\nE. Work needs to be done against self-induced e.m.f. in establishing the current.\n\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below:"}, "options": [{"id": "2a445b", "text": "$\\mathrm{A}, \\mathrm{B}, \\mathrm{C}, \\mathrm{E}$ only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb6e"}, {"id": "d8ee5e", "text": "B, C, D, E only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb6f"}, {"id": "7a1482", "text": "$\\mathrm{A}, \\mathrm{C}, \\mathrm{D}, \\mathrm{E}$ only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb70"}, {"id": "dc6a00", "text": "A, B, C, D only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb71"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb72", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f87fe"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87ce"], "question": {"text": "A coil of self inductance <math><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> and resistance of <math><mn>0.1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> is connected through a switch to a battery of internal resistance <math><mtext>&#160;</mtext><mn>0.9</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> . After the switch is closed, the time taken for the current to attain <math><mn>80</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">%</mi></math> of the saturation value is:&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mrow><mo>[</mo> <mrow> <mi>ln</mi><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1.6</mn></mrow> <mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow> </math>"}, "options": [{"id": "e1b4b8", "text": "<math><mn>0.103</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb73"}, {"id": "155737", "text": "<math><mn>0.002</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb74"}, {"id": "e8d639", "text": "<math><mn>0.324</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb75"}, {"id": "403c81", "text": "<math><mn>0.016</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb76"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb77", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60ced5dc19d2aa2b78a3a76c"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8ed4"], "question": {"text": "Consider the LR circuit shown in the figure. If the switch S is closed at <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> then the amount of charge that passes through the battery between <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> is:<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F527efd6a-63ca-4856-8941-456360a46842-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 290px; height: 177px;\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "66dd45", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>7.3</mn><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb78"}, {"id": "2daac7", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>7.3</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb79"}, {"id": "7adc3f", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2.7</mn><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb7a"}, {"id": "f90006", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2.7</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb7b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb7c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e0"], "concepts": ["60e5678c499d1e49588f9257"], "question": {"text": "A planar loop of wire rotates in a uniform magnetic field. Initially, at <math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> , the plane of the loop is perpendicular to the magnetic field. If it rotates with a period of <math><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> about an axis in its plane then the magnitude of induced emf will be maximum and minimum, respectively at:"}, "options": [{"id": "ace37a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2.5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7.5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb7d"}, {"id": "77d8e1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2.5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5.0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb7e"}, {"id": "ef655b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5.0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7.5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb7f"}, {"id": "0eefd8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5.0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb80"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb81", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1e66f9ce3f243b4b18"], "question": {"text": "Consider \\(\\mathrm{I}_1\\) and \\(\\mathrm{I}_2\\) are the currents flowing simultaneously in two nearby coils 1 & 2, respectively. If \\(\\mathrm{L}_1=\\) self inductance of coil \\(1, \\mathrm{M}_{12}=\\) mutual inductance of coil 1 with respect to coil 2, then the value of induced emf in coil 1 will be\nOptions"}, "options": [{"id": "feddfb", "text": "\\(\\varepsilon_1=-L_1 \\frac{\\mathrm{dI}_2}{d t}-\\mathrm{M}_{12} \\frac{\\mathrm{dI}_1}{d t}\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb82"}, {"id": "396ae2", "text": "\\(\\varepsilon_1=-L_1 \\frac{\\mathrm{dI}_1}{d t}-\\mathrm{M}_{12} \\frac{\\mathrm{dI}_2}{d t}\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb83"}, {"id": "89ca85", "text": "\\(\\varepsilon_1=-L_1 \\frac{\\mathrm{dI}_1}{d t}-\\mathrm{M}_{12} \\frac{\\mathrm{dI}_1}{d t}\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb84"}, {"id": "37d2ba", "text": "\\(\\varepsilon_1=-L_1 \\frac{\\mathrm{dI}_1}{d t}+\\mathrm{M}_{12} \\frac{\\mathrm{dI}_2}{\\mathrm{dt}}\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb85"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb86", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b89"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b5c"], "question": {"text": "<p>A metallic rod of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math>&nbsp;is rotated with an angular speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi></math>&nbsp;normal to a uniform magnetic field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;about an axis passing through one end of rod as shown in figure. The induced emf will be :</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Ff95adc92-8a37-4e1a-949b-9f146a236eb1-9893978.PNG?alt=media\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 242px;\" />.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "6ebd01", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#969;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb87"}, {"id": "448379", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#969;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb88"}, {"id": "fb7702", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#969;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb89"}, {"id": "9e8784", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>L</mi><mi>&#969;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb8a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb8b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e0"], "concepts": ["60ced5db19d2aa2b78a3a73a"], "question": {"text": "The magnetic flux through a coil perpendicular to its plane is varying according to the relation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> Weber. If the resistance of the coil is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ohm</mi></math>, then the induced current through the coil at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> will be,"}, "options": [{"id": "3a4a9b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb8c"}, {"id": "de513e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb8d"}, {"id": "486f89", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>17</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb8e"}, {"id": "6d351c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>18</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926eb8f"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:45.526Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:45.526Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926ebd7"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926ebd5", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926ebb9", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e0"], "concepts": ["60e5678c499d1e49588f9257"], "question": {"text": "The magnetic flux <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ϕ</mi></math> (in weber) linked with a closed circuit of resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo> </mo><mi>Ω</mi></math> varies with time (in seconds) as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>36</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. The induced current in the circuit at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo> </mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> is _______ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "9abdfc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926ebba"}, {"id": "11dd9a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926ebbb"}, {"id": "5bf258", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926ebbc"}, {"id": "85ba39", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926ebbd"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926ebbe", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b89"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95c4"], "question": {"text": "<p>A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;long metal rod <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></math> completes the circuit as shown in figure. The plane of the circuit is perpendicular to the magnetic field of flux density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>. If the resistance of the circuit is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8486;</mo></math>, the force needed to move the rod in direction, as indicated, with a constant speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> will be _______<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fd1f383d4-9dbb-40b0-b719-5a9d3262d9ac.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 157px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "e70690", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926ebbf"}, {"id": "d1d71c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926ebc0"}, {"id": "4d99af", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926ebc1"}, {"id": "9a3cbf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926ebc2"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926ebc3", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5e"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b564a"], "question": {"text": "In a fluorescent lamp choke (a small transformer) <math><mn>100</mn><mi></mi><mi>V</mi></math> of reverse voltage is produced when the choke current changes uniformly from <math><mn>0.25</mn><mi></mi><mi>A</mi></math> to <math><mn>0</mn></math> in a duration of <math><mn>0.025</mn><mi></mi><mi>m</mi><mi>s</mi></math> . The self-inductance of the choke (in <math><mi>m</mi><mi>H</mi></math> ) is estimated to be ________"}, "options": [{"id": "037754", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926ebc4"}, {"id": "18d26e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926ebc5"}, {"id": "4e0363", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926ebc6"}, {"id": "e488c3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926ebc7"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926ebc8", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60ced5dc19d2aa2b78a3a76c"], "concepts": ["60ced5db19d2aa2b78a3a740"], "question": {"text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Ff-NI79HHyNcR8eD4hvFRHEfA7_vImqGIrxrVefadkVs.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>\nIn the given circuit the sliding contact is pulled outwards such that electric current in the circuit changes at the rate of $8 \\mathrm{~A} / \\mathrm{s}$. At an instant when R is $12 \\Omega$, the value of the current in the circuit will be ______ A."}, "options": [{"id": "660fd9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926ebc9"}, {"id": "eed72f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926ebca"}, {"id": "d04e40", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926ebcb"}, {"id": "e7a3f9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926ebcc"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926ebcd", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b566e"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5644"], "question": {"text": "A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mH</mi></math> coil carrying constant current is connected to a battery of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> through a switch. Now after switch is opened current becomes zero in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. The average e.m.f. induced in the coil is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "3fff07", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926ebce"}, {"id": "70a3ec", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926